  "cause": "PC-relative data reads used the discovery lane, which guessed a scalar prefix from one expanded field despite an existing full pointer owner. The observer for established pointer descriptors only walked An-based reads. Plain PC-displacement reads also inherited a fabricated D0 index identity.",
  "implementation": [
    "Factor the existing clean pointer-descriptor lookup and reuse one descriptor-to-consumer factory for PC- and An-based reads. No target address/name rule or second transfer engine.",
    "Keep discovery and observation distinct. Early discovery does not create a scalar prefix under a known pointer owner. The final observation pass sees both projected record owners and existing native pointer-table declarations, retaining every actual reader.",
    "Carry decoded Dn/An index identity and actual destination register, along with the existing mask/compare/loop evidence. Structural entry count remains separate from a runtime index domain.",
    "Plain PC displacement has no index register. The new pointer observer handles brief indexed addressing and leaves suppressed/indirect/full-extension cases outside its admitted scope.",
    "Do not promote pointee targets, reclassify original bytes, rename storage, discard leaf domains, infer an incoming edge or force runtime state."
  ],
